  "verbalization": "Morolic Acid appears to have a complex relationship with TAR DNA-binding protein 43, as evidenced by its indirect targeting of this protein through multiple pathways. The first pathway links Morolic Acid to Asialoglycoprotein receptor 2, which is then targeted by Mollicelline K, a compound that ultimately affects TAR DNA-binding protein 43. The second pathway reveals that Morolic Acid also targets Multidrug resistance-associated protein 7, which is itself targeted by a complex organic compound that also influences TAR DNA-binding protein 43. These findings suggest that Morolic Acid may act through different molecular mechanisms to modulate the activity of TAR DNA-binding protein 43, potentially through the indirect activation of downstream targets. The shared involvement of TAR DNA-binding protein 43 in both pathways implies a possible functional role in the biological processes affected by these compounds, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
